# Local data directories at the repository root only. Unanchored, this pattern
# also matched src/tradeit/data/, which silently excluded the entire data
# package -- providers, registry, quality, validation universe and the offline
# package importer -- from every commit. A fresh clone did not build.
/data/
/var/
*.db
*.sqlite3
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Acquired market data.
#
# Narrowly scoped on purpose. An earlier unanchored `data/` rule in this file
# also matched `src/tradeit/data/` and silently kept the entire data package out
# of every commit; a fresh clone did not build. Every pattern below is either
# anchored to the repository root (leading `/`) or names a directory that no
# source tree uses (`_acquisition`).
#
# LICENSING: market-data licences commonly forbid redistribution. Do not push
# bulk vendor data to a public repository unless the licence explicitly permits
# it. Source code, manifests, small deterministic fixtures and validation
# reports are fine; the raw vendor responses and the bar files are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The acquisition workspace: raw vendor responses, journal, adjusted-price
# sidecar. Lives inside a package directory and is always vendor data.
**/_acquisition/

# Acquisition output directories at the repository ROOT only.
#
# The leading `/` is doing the important work. `empirical-*/` unanchored would
# match any directory anywhere whose name starts with "empirical"; anchored, it
# matches only children of the repository root, which is where the CLI's
# `--output` conventionally points. Nothing under `src/`, `docs/` or `tests/`
# can be caught by it, and `git check-ignore` is run against those paths in the
# test suite so the guarantee is enforced rather than asserted in a comment.
#
# Covers /empirical-smoke/, /empirical-smoke-2/, /empirical-smoke-fmp/,
# /empirical-validation-2010-2026/ and anything else following the convention.
/empirical-*/
/market-data/
/packages/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local diagnostic and validation output.
#
# `tradeit scan --json <path>` and `tradeit validate --json <path>` take a path
# the operator chooses, and the documented examples used to be bare filenames --
# `--json out.json`, `--json report.json` -- which land in whatever directory the
# command was run from. Run from a clone, that is the repository root, and a
# diagnostic session leaves scan-*.json, validation-report-*.json and redirected
# .log files sitting next to pyproject.toml as untracked clutter.
#
# `/out/` is the one place those belong. The documentation now points there and
# the CLI creates it on demand.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED, AND WHY. Not `*.json`: the curated identity
# evidence in docs/research/ is a .json file, it is the research output rather
# than a rebuildable artifact, and a blanket rule would hide it the way the old
# unanchored `data/` rule hid src/tradeit/data/. Not `*.log`, `scan-*` or
# `validation-*` either -- each would silently swallow a future source file,
# fixture or document whose name happens to match. The rule is narrow on
# purpose: one root-anchored directory, chosen for output, ignored entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/out/

# The research-01 local corpus and its backfill checkpoint. Named exactly, not
# globbed: `*.sqlite3` above does not cover `research01.sqlite`, which is how
# a 16,000-row vendor corpus nearly became a tracked file. Downloaded vendor
# data is never committed, and a checkpoint is operational state, not evidence.
/research01.sqlite
# SQLite's own journal and WAL sidecars for it. They appear whenever a write is
# in flight and are not evidence of anything.
/research01.sqlite-journal
/research01.sqlite-wal
/research01.sqlite-shm
#
# Every research-01 checkpoint, by one anchored pattern rather than by name.
#
# This replaced an enumerated list plus a `/.research01_*shard*.json` glob. The
# enumeration failed exactly as its own comment predicted: 56 shard files were
# committed before the glob was written, and three more --
# .research01_confirm_delta.json, .research01_dead_tickers_pass4.json and
# .research01_live_backfill.json -- were never covered by any rule at all,
# because each new run coins a filename nobody thought to add. All 59 were
# published when the repository went public on 2026-09-19. They contained only
# SEC CIKs and tickers, so nothing secret escaped, but a checkpoint is
# operational state and a rule that requires remembering to extend it is not a
# rule.
#
# REJECTED ALTERNATIVE: a bare `.research01_*` with no `/` and no `.json`. It
# would also match a future src/tradeit/research01_*.py module, which is the
# precise shape of the unanchored `data/` defect this file already carries two
# warnings about. The leading `/` confines it to the repository root and the
# `.json` suffix confines it to checkpoints; `tests/unit/test_repository_hygiene.py`
# asserts both halves rather than trusting this comment.
#
# An ignore rule does not untrack a file that is already committed. Adding a
# pattern here is half the fix; `git rm --cached` is the other half.
/.research01_*.json
